tgs:Monologue.Frankly_151_Part6PlanningUnderUncertainty a thinkr:Episode, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeType thinkr:EpisodeType.Monologue ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeSegment tgs:EpisodeSegment.Frankly ;
    skos:prefLabel "Protect the Irreversible: What Matters Most in an Uncertain Future? | How to Think About the Future Pt 6"@en ;
    skos:definition "The series' closer - a methodology for individual/community planning and action given the 4-Dimension framework, rather than a specific list of recommended actions. Opens with a type-1/type-2-error framing (false positives vs. false negatives in how people respond to uncertain threats) as a lens for thinking about failure modes in planning, before laying out Hagens' own approach to prioritizing action under deep uncertainty."@en ;
    thinkr:hasHost tgs:Persona.NateHagens ;
    dct:isPartOf tgs:Series.HowToThinkAboutTheFuture ;
    thinkr:seriesPosition 6 ;
    dct:created "2026-07-05"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2026-07-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior ;
    thinkr:hasCanonicalSource <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/frankly-original/151-protect-the-irreversible> ;
    thinkr:hasTranscript <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Frankly-151-Transcript-How-to-Think-About-the-Future-Part-6.pdf> ;
    thinkr:hasReplay <https://youtu.be/bMfzVhTWMDM> ;
    thinkr:discusses tgs:Concept.ScenarioThinking, tgs:Concept.UnicornStrategies, tgs:Concept.Superorganism, tgs:Scenario.GS-CI-FN-SW, tgs:Scenario.MO-CD-GD-QU, tgs:Scenario.GS-FF-CW-HT, tgs:Scenario.MM-FF-CW-CB ;
    dct:references tgs:Monologue.Frankly_129_DesperatelySeekingAgency, tgs:Monologue.Frankly_132_FrameworkForAction, tgs:Monologue.Frankly_142_GuideToStayingHumanPart2, tgs:Monologue.Frankly_97_TheSuperorganismIn7Minutes ;
    skos:scopeNote "MAJOR CORRECTION 2026-08-13: same class of error as Frankly_150 — this episode's skos:prefLabel, thinkr:hasCanonicalSource, and hasTranscript month were all wrong since first built, never verified against the real page until now. Corrected via direct fetch."@en ;
